# The lowest version the next release tag may take (Issue #808).
#
# `.github/workflows/release-tag.yml` automates the PATCH number only. This
# file is the one line a human edits to move the series: a floor above the
# newest release tag makes the next merge to `main` mint the floor exactly,
# and once that release exists the floor is below the series again and patch
# increments continue from it (1.3.0 -> 1.3.1).
#
# 1.6.0 records the post-run callback contract change that 1.5.170 shipped
# unannounced (callback schema 2, Issues #2039 #2041): the contract is now
# stated as additive-only, the schema 1 field set is pinned by test, and a
# callback-failure report closes itself when the hook recovers.
#
# 1.7.0 carries the whole RTK Bash-output switch — the `rtk_output.enabled`
# config block, the pinned RTK toolchain, the five wired paths, the `RTK:`
# stats line and the `rtk` callback block (milestone #2328).
#
# 1.8.0 turns RTK output filtering on by default (Issue #2432): a host that
# never wrote `rtk_output` now filters, and `enabled: false` is the opt-out.
#
# 1.9.0 moves the top model tier from Fable to Opus 5.5 (Issue #2560): the
# eight planning-shaped phases default to `opus`, the container pins Claude
# Code 2.1.281, and `CLAUDE_MODEL_PLANNING=fable` is the rollback.
1.9.0
